BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Readers' Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T180000
UID:6a90745ca967887492bc5103@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:2nd & 4th Tuesdays\, 2-4 pm in the OCA Lobby\nInterested in le
 arning\, sharing and reading short plays? Readers Theatre is a fun opportu
 nity to express yourself.\nReaders Theatre participants read scripts adapt
 ed from literature\, while the ‘audience’ pictures the action by heari
 ng the script being read aloud. It requires no sets\, costumes\, props\, o
 r memorized lines. Instead of acting literature as in a play\, the perform
 er’s goal is to read a script aloud effectively\, enabling the audience 
 to visualize the action. Performers bring the text alive by using voice\, 
 facial expressions\, and some gestures. $15 participation fee\, $10 for OC
 A members.\nAlternating READER’S CHOICE nights: Can be play\, poetry\, s
 tory\, essay\, your own writing\, OR ??????\nFor more information\, email\
 nJoan Ambrosini\,\ncoordinator .
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/readers-the
 atre-2-m26cd-ntb9s-k5mxf
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Bath with Laura Benson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T203000
UID:69ade383c638f84c8457b18e@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Rest & Renew at our Sound Bath!\nSupport your nervous system\,
  release anxiety and stress\, and harmonize your body\, mind and spirit on
  the 2nd Tuesday of every month! Laura Benson has a Masters in Intuition M
 edicine(R) and is a certified sound healer who will guide you through a ge
 ntle meditation before each sound bath session. Bring your own yoga mat & 
 blanket and come ready to rest and renew! In the OCA Studio.\nSliding scal
 e pricing $25-$35.\nRegister\nA sound bath is a whole-body\, immersive lis
 tening experience. During a sound bath\, participants often sit or lie dow
 n\, and are surrounded by the mostly non-melodic soundscapes created by a 
 range of instruments played by the sound bath facilitator. Hence\, they ar
 e “bathed” in sound.\nSound therapy is a non-invasive healing modality
  that utilizes the physical and physiological interactions of sound on our
  bodies and nervous systems to produce therapeutic results. In a sound hea
 ling session\, specific sonic frequencies are used to soothe the central n
 ervous system\, calm the breath\, and quiet the mind by encouraging the br
 ain to move into more relaxed states\, down from beta (fight-or-flight) an
 d into theta and alpha waves. This increases present-moment awareness and 
 reduces stress and anxiety. Sound baths have been found to be effective in
  improving mood\, cognitive function\, and overall mental\, physical\, and
  spiritual wellbeing.\nCrystal bowl sound baths are particularly powerful 
 in that each bowl is tuned to a specific frequency that corresponds with a
  different chakra\, or energy center\, of the body. Based on specific need
 s\, a practitioner can focus on releasing tension or clearing out stuck en
 ergy in specific chakras by playing certain bowls or intervals.\nWhile att
 ending a sound bath\, you may experience physical sensations brought out b
 y the crystal sound bowls or gong\, such as tingling in your limbs or scal
 p\, slowing of your breathing\, eye flutters\, or small muscle spasms. Not
  to worry! These sensations often indicate the release of tension or emoti
 onal energy stored in the body’s energy systems.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/rest-renew-
 monthly-sound-bath-l5n5c-wchlw-38gmc-rw262-hd6w3-nlnhm-bn8b8-d74pg-d79je-w
 x3an-ampe7-zckp7-gndtj-32c6f-4y8an-wsmxr-y3rtb-8k62p-lx4gx-36kl7-5kgyd-tbe
 tg-2kydp
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
