BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gradina - Balkan Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T210000
UID:6a9080bd2610bd4e2d6a212a@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Gradina is a Balkan music ensemble based in California’s Nor
 th Bay area.\nWe celebrate the seasons and their festivals through song an
 d dance\, bringing Old World rituals to new light and new generations to r
 evel in the staying power of gratitude for life on Earth.\nWe sing both a 
 cappella and with instrumental accompaniment. We lean toward traditional s
 ongs and arrangements. We present “sit-down” concerts for choral liste
 ning as well as dance concerts\, and we are also available to teach most o
 f the dances we present. We are honored to play with many Balkan musicians
  from near and far\, and every concert is different\, often with a differe
 nt array of performers alongside the core group.\nOur special guests will 
 be Gaelen Genetti on Bulgarian kaval and Christina Penrose on clarinet.\nT
 ickets are $25/$15 for OCA members. Doors open at 6:30 PM.\nGet Tickets
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/gradina-bal
 kan-music
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Autumn Muses: Marjorie Stein\, Kathleen Winter\, Todd Melicker\, C
 laire Drucker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T160000
UID:6a908338f764e353b2662a7e@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Occidental Center for the Arts Literary Series presents\nAutum
 n Muses\n\, An Afternoon with poets\, Marjorie Stein\, Kathleen Winter\, C
 laire Drucker and Todd Melicker.\nJoin us for a relaxed Autumn afternoon o
 f poetry from our four esteemed poet friends\, with tea and cookies! This 
 free event will include selected readings by each poet\, with handpan inte
 rludes from Judith Lerner\, followed by audience Q&A\, book sales & signin
 g.\nAbout the Poets\nMarjorie Stein\nis the author of\nunRavel\,\nwhich wa
 s selected by Elaine Equi for the 2025 Marsh Hawk Press Poetry Prize\nAn A
 tlas of Lost Causes\,\nMarjorie’s first book\, was published by Kelsey S
 treet Press in 2011. Another poetry project\,\nIn the Hinges of the World\
 n\, was shortlisted for the Lost Horse Press 2020 Idaho Prize for Poetry. 
 Her work has appeared\, or is forthcoming in\nAmerican Poetry Journal\, Bl
 ood Orange Review\, The Denver Quarterly\, Interim\, Marsh Hawk Press Chap
 ter One Series\, Mary\, New American Writing\, VOLT\,\nand other publicati
 ons. Marjorie lives in Northern California\, with her wife\, where she is 
 privileged to spend time playing with words.\nwww.marjoriestein.org\nKathl
 een Winter\nis the author of\nTransformer\, I will not kick my friends\,\n
 and\nNostalgia for the Criminal Past.\nHer collection\nSerial Fabulist\nis
  forthcoming from Texas Review Press in early 2027. Her poems have appeare
 d in\nThe New Republic\, The New Statesman\, Cincinnati Review\, Agni\, Ya
 le Review\, Gulf Coast\, Tupelo Quarterly\,\nand\nMichigan Quarterly Revie
 w.\nHer work has been supported by fellowships from the Texas Institute of
  Letters\, the University of Texas at Austin\, Heinrich Böll Cottage\, Ma
 ison Dora Maar\, Cill Rialaig Project\, James Merrill House\, and the Sewa
 nee Writers’ Conference. Awards include the Poetry Society of America Th
 e Writer Magazine/Emily Dickinson Award and the Rochelle Ratner Memorial P
 rize. Kathleen lives in Glen Ellen\, California.\nClaire Drucker\nis the c
 urrent Sonoma County Poet Laureate. She is a Jewish lesbian mom\, educatio
 nal consultant\, poet\, and dancer. Her first book-length collection of po
 ems\,\nThe Life You Gave Me\n\, was published in 2023 by Kelsay Books. Her
  chapbook\,\nThe Fluid Body\,\nwas published in 2014 by Finishing Line Pre
 ss. Claire’s poems have been published in numerous journals\, including\
 nCA Quarterly\, Jewish Literary Journal\, Rust & Moth\, Epiphany\, Puerto 
 del Sol\nand\nWomen Artists Datebook.\nShe taught English at Santa Rosa Ju
 nior College for many years and was also a poet-teacher with\nCA Poets in 
 the Schools. She is currently the poetry curator for The Sitting Room\, a 
 community library dedicated to women’s literature and art in Penngrove.\
 nTodd Melicker\nis the author of\nrendezvous\n(Winner of the Black Box Poe
 try Prize\, Rescue Press) and\nis this the body / if hovers\n(lyric& Press
 ). Originally from the Northern Sierra\, he lives with his family in Sonom
 a County.
